---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
const avatar = 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131162811?v=4';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Aleksandar and JustDaddit" description="Why Aleksandar Spasevski created JustDaddit and how the site helps families choose expensive gear without invented testing or generic recommendations." canonicalPath="/about/">
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About' }]} /><p class="eyebrow">The person behind the homework</p><h1>About JustDaddit</h1><p class="page-lede">I built this for the moment when a fun family idea turns into eighteen tabs, four incompatible batteries, and no clear answer.</p></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="shell about-grid"><figure class="founder-photo"><img src={avatar} alt="Aleksandar Spasevski, founder of JustDaddit" width="460" height="460" /><figcaption>Aleksandar Spasevski · founder, father, and obsessive pre-purchase researcher</figcaption></figure><article class="reading"><p class="eyebrow">Hello, I’m Aleksandar</p><h2>I like the fun part. I also read the manual.</h2><p class="lead">JustDaddit is a family gear publication for parents who want the useful answer before spending serious money.</p><p>I am a father, marketer, and researcher based in Skopje. My professional life taught me how to organize large amounts of messy information. Family life taught me that none of it matters if the answer ignores the child, the parent, the available space, the cleanup, or the second weekend.</p><p>This site begins with research reviews because I do not own the full product catalog. That is a limitation, and hiding it would be dishonest. A rigorous desk review can still answer important questions about exact models, compatibility, starting cost, parts, manuals, warranties, owner-report patterns, and recalls. It cannot tell you what my hands felt on the transmitter or how a truck survived my driveway.</p><p>When JustDaddit completes hands-on work, the evidence label changes. Until then, every page tells you what was researched, what remains uncertain, and why I reached the verdict.</p><h3>Why “JustDaddit”?</h3><p>Because family plans often begin with somebody saying, “Dad, can we…?” Then the adult has to turn excitement into a workable choice. The name is about that role, not about excluding mothers, grandparents, guardians, or anyone else who does the same homework.</p><p>JustDaddit is independent and is not affiliated with Reddit or its r/daddit community.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="section decision-panel"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading"><p>What I owe the reader</p><div class="heading-copy"><h2>Four promises</h2></div></div><div class="principle-grid"><article class="principle"><h3>Name the evidence</h3><p>I will not call research testing or turn an owner comment into a statistic.</p></article><article class="principle"><h3>Show the real cost</h3><p>The battery, charger, installation, accessories, and maintenance belong in the decision.</p></article><article class="principle"><h3>Say who should skip it</h3><p>A recommendation without an exclusion is usually advertising with better grammar.</p></article><article class="principle"><h3>Correct the record</h3><p>Model generations, prices, recalls, and support change. Pages need visible dates and updates.</p></article></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="shell finder-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h2>The family is real. The children are not content assets.</h2></div><div><p>I may write about the practical reality of family life and describe age-appropriate buying situations. My children’s identities and private lives stay protected. A good product decision does not require turning them into public proof.</p><p>The author photograph and opinions on this site are mine. Any future contributor, owner verifier, or tester will be named and their relationship to the product disclosed.</p><a class="button alt" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}how-we-research/`}>Read the research standard</a></div></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
